    "b-ag-d1": {
      "id": "b-ag-d1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": board-level target selection is deterministic scheduler code, not an agent; a worker session receives exactly one already-claimed epoch target. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": a director agent with a board-level prompt was rejected; deterministic ranking is auditable and spends no model calls on routing. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the worker and any future run-phase agent, which must also receive claimed work rather than choose it."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ag-d2": {
      "id": "b-ag-d2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the worker stays inside its target claim and category-typed write set; widening happens only through an evidence-backed checkpoint-note request that the runner decides, and validation state is runner-owned. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": agent self-widening and agent-owned validation were rejected; write safety and durable evidence stay with deterministic code. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the worker and any future agent that edits game source."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ag-d3": {
      "id": "b-ag-d3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision: integration conflicts use deterministic outcome records and target requeueing. No integration-resolver agent merges them. The epoch boundary may invoke a separate Codex build-fixer for a build failure, with a five-minute timeout and patch validation. Why: conflict disposition and build repair have different triggers and validation rules. Applies to: the running scheduler and epoch boundary."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ag-d4": {
      "id": "b-ag-d4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision: librarian-v2 consumes index tasks and backfill-librarian researches one target at a time. Both return proposals to the shared apply layer. Their agent pages specify the current schema differences. Why: separate entry points give event-driven curation and target-driven research distinct contexts while sharing validation. Applies to: the two librarian agents and future knowledge agents."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ag-build-fixer-note": {
      "id": "b-ag-build-fixer-note",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The four-entry catalog is not an inventory of every model invocation. The epoch build-fixer is a direct bounded Codex invocation outside this catalog, owned by the epoch boundary."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
